      "timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:02:12.745Z",
      "message": "This one is rung 1 on the ladder — session lifetime is security posture, so I want your yes before I touch it rather than after.\n\nThe change itself is trivial: `config.js:3`, `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30` → `480`. `server.js` just reads the value, so nothing else needs to change.\n\nWhat that 16× extension means:\n- A stolen session token (shared/unlocked laptop, XSS, leaked cookie) stays usable for a full working day instead of half an hour.\n- Idle sessions on unattended machines stay live across lunch, meetings, and a commute.\n- If this is idle timeout rather than absolute lifetime, a user touching the app periodically never re-authenticates at all.\n\nWorth knowing before you answer: a common middle path is keeping the idle timeout short (30–60 min) while raising the absolute session cap to 8 hours, or adding a refresh-token/sliding-window so people stop getting logged out mid-task without leaving stolen tokens valid all day. That's a design choice, not a value swap — if you want to go that route, say so and we'll brainstorm it.\n\nSay go and I'll make the one-line change as asked.",
